18:["$","section","1",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-3 font-display text-xl font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Author's purpose: why the text exists"}],[["$","p","0",{"className":"mb-3 max-w-[68ch] text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-eng-navy-800","children":"Every text is written to do something. The four purposes you will see most often are to inform, to persuade, to entertain, and to explain how something works. A single text can have more than one, but TABE items usually ask for the primary purpose."}]],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mb-4 max-w-[68ch] space-y-2","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"To inform — presents facts with little evaluation. Neutral vocabulary."}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"To persuade — argues for a position. Look for claims, evidence, and words carrying judgment."}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"To explain / instruct — walks through a process or a mechanism, often in sequence."}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"To entertain — tells a story for its own sake, with narrative detail and voice."}]]}]]}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 max-w-[68ch] rounded-lg border-l-4 border-eng-gold-500 bg-eng-gold-50 p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-gold-700","children":"Test tip"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":"Ask what the author wants you to do after reading. Know something? Do something? Agree with something? Feel something? The answer to that question is the purpose."}]]}]]}]
19:["$","section","2",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-3 font-display text-xl font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Fact and opinion"}],[["$","p","0",{"className":"mb-3 max-w-[68ch] text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-eng-navy-800","children":"A fact can be checked against a record, a measurement, or a source — whether or not it turns out to be true. An opinion expresses a judgment and cannot be verified, even when most people share it."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"mb-3 max-w-[68ch] text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-eng-navy-800","children":"Be careful: an opinion is not the same as a lie, and a fact is not the same as a correct statement. \"The office received 4,000 requests in June\" is a factual statement, verifiable and possibly wrong. \"The office is doing an excellent job\" is an opinion no record can settle."}]],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mb-4 max-w-[68ch] space-y-2","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Opinion markers: best, worst, should, ought, unfair, remarkable, too much."}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Fact markers: dates, counts, measurements, named sources, quoted records."}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Watch for opinions written to sound like facts: \"Everyone knows that…\" is a judgment wearing a fact's clothing."}]]}]]}],"$undefined","$undefined"]}]
1a:["$","section",null,{"id":"see-it","className":"scroll-mt-32 border-t border-eng-navy-200 pt-10","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-2 flex items-center gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-eng-navy-800 text-sm font-bold text-white","aria-hidden":"true","children":2}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-eng-teal-700","children":"See It"}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl font-bold text-eng-navy-900 sm:text-3xl","children":"A worked example"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 max-w-[68ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":"Watch the reasoning before you try it. Notice the order of the moves — that order is the skill."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"One event, two points of view"}],["$","article",null,{"className":"rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white shadow-sm","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"border-b border-eng-navy-100 px-4 py-4 sm:px-6","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"The Bus Route Hearing"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"rounded-full bg-eng-teal-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-eng-teal-800","children":"Informational"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs text-eng-navy-400","children":[161," words"]}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-4 py-5 sm:px-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[68ch] space-y-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":["$undefined",["$","span",null,{"children":"ACCOUNT ONE — from a transit agency newsletter: At Tuesday's public hearing, the agency presented its plan to consolidate the B14 and B16 routes. Consolidation would reduce duplicated service along a fourteen-block overlap and allow the agency to increase frequency on the combined route from every twenty minutes to every twelve. Thirty-one residents attended. Agency staff answered questions for ninety minutes and will accept written comment for thirty days."}]]}],["$","p","1",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":["$undefined",["$","span",null,{"children":"ACCOUNT TWO — from a letter to a neighborhood paper: I sat through Tuesday's hearing on the B14 and B16. The agency called it consolidation. What it means for my block is that the stop two doors from my building disappears, and the nearest one becomes an eight-block walk. I am 71. Eight blocks in February is not a shorter wait; it is no bus at all. Thirty-one of us came out on a weeknight. They took our questions politely and told us the comment period would be open for thirty days."}]]}]]}],"$undefined",["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 border-t border-eng-navy-100 pt-3 text-xs italic text-eng-navy-400","children":"Original passage — BEOC Academic Bridge"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-xl border-2 border-eng-teal-600 bg-white p-4 sm:p-6","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-teal-700","children":"The question"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-lg font-semibold leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":"How does point of view shape the way each account presents the same hearing?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 mt-6 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-teal-700","children":"Thinking it through"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-8 w-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-eng-teal-700 text-sm font-bold text-white","aria-hidden":"true","children":1}],"$L22"]}],"$L23","$L24","$L25","$L26"]}],"$L27","$L28"]}]]}]]}]
