processed in the following cycle, which means your hours will appear on the next paycheck rather than the current one. Keep a copy of your submission confirmation until the corresponding paycheck arrives."}]]}]]}],"$undefined",["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 border-t border-eng-navy-100 pt-3 text-xs italic text-eng-navy-400","children":"Original passage — BEOC Academic Bridge"}]]}]]}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","$L29","pov-g1",{"question":{"id":"pov-g1","type":"multiple-choice","question":"What is the point of view and the author's primary purpose in this passage?","passageId":"pov-guided-manual","choices":["First person; to persuade employees that the payroll system is fair","Second person; to instruct employees on how and when to submit time sheets","Third person limited; to describe the payroll department's workload","Second person; to entertain employees with a story about payroll"],"correctAnswer":1,"hint":"Look at the pronouns first, then ask what the author wants you to do after reading.","explanation":"The passage addresses the reader directly as you, and every sentence tells the reader what to do or what will happen if they do not. That is second person, written to instruct.","choiceRationales":["There is no I anywhere, and the passage never argues that anything is fair.","Correct. Direct address plus procedural steps and consequences.","No character's thoughts appear, and the payroll department's workload is never discussed.","The point of view is right, but nothing here is a story or written for enjoyment."],"skill":"point-of-view","difficulty":"Foundation"},"number":1}]]}]]}]]}]
1c:["$","section",null,{"id":"practice","className":"scroll-mt-32 border-t border-eng-navy-200 pt-10","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-2 flex items-center gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-eng-navy-800 text-sm font-bold text-white","aria-hidden":"true","children":4}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-eng-teal-700","children":"Practice"}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl font-bold text-eng-navy-900 sm:text-3xl","children":"Practice on a full passage"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 max-w-[68ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":"A longer passage with several questions. Check each answer as you go."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":["$undefined",[["$","article","pov-practice-library",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white shadow-sm","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"border-b border-eng-navy-100 px-4 py-4 sm:px-6","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"What the Library Became"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"rounded-full bg-eng-teal-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-eng-teal-800","children":"Argument"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs text-eng-navy-400","children":[171," words"]}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-4 py-5 sm:px-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[68ch] space-y-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":1}],["$","span",null,{"children":"The branch library on my corner circulated 41,000 items last year. It also hosted 312 public programs, provided 9,400 sessions on its public computers, and served as a designated cooling center on eleven days."}]]}],["$","p","1",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":2}],["$","span",null,{"children":"City budget discussions still describe library funding as spending on books. That description is decades out of date, and it quietly makes the case for cuts. If a library is a book warehouse, then a city with declining print circulation has an obvious place to save money."}]]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":3}],["$","span",null,{"children":"But the computer sessions are not incidental. For a resident applying for a job, renewing a benefit, or filing a form that no longer exists on paper, the branch is often the only free place to sit down with a keyboard and get help using it."}]]}],["$","p","3",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":4}],["$","span",null,{"children":"I do not think the library should be exempt from budget scrutiny. Every department should have to justify what it costs. I think the justification should be measured against what the library actually does, and the current accounting does not measure that at all."}]]}]]}],"$undefined",["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 border-t border-eng-navy-100 pt-3 text-xs italic text-eng-navy-400","children":"Original passage — BEOC Academic Bridge"}]]}]]}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":["$L2a","$L2b","$L2c"]}]]}]]}]
1d:["$","section",null,{"id":"challenge","className":"scroll-mt-32 border-t border-eng-navy-200 pt-10","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-2 flex items-center gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-eng-navy-800 text-sm font-bold text-white","aria-hidden":"true","children":5}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-eng-teal-700","children":"Challenge"}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl font-bold text-eng-navy-900 sm:text-3xl","children":"A harder, TABE-style set"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 max-w-[68ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":"Denser text and less obvious answers — closer to what the test will ask of you."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"max-w-[68ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":"This biography is built on facts you could look up, but its author is not neutral about the person. Read all five paragraphs before you decide what the author is trying to do, and test each sentence by asking whether a record could settle it."}],[["$","article","pov-challenge-perkins",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white shadow-sm","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"border-b border-eng-navy-100 px-4 py-4 sm:px-6","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"What Frances Perkins Saw"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"rounded-full bg-eng-teal-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-eng-teal-800","children":"Biography"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs text-eng-navy-400","children":[348," words"]}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-4 py-5 sm:px-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[68ch] space-y-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":1}],["$","span",null,{"children":"On a Saturday afternoon in March 1911, a young advocate for working people named Frances Perkins was near Washington Square in New York City when fire broke out at the Triangle Shirtwaist Factory, on the upper floors of a nearby building. She reached the street in time to see workers trapped at the windows. More than one hundred people died, most of them young immigrant women. Perkins spent the rest of her career acting on what she saw that day."}]]}],["$","p","1",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":2}],["$","span",null,{"children":"In the following years, she investigated factory conditions for New York State and pushed for laws on fire safety and working hours. When Franklin Roosevelt became governor of New York, he made her the state's industrial commissioner, in charge of its labor department. It is hard to imagine a better preparation for what came next."}]]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":3}],["$","span",null,{"children":"When Roosevelt became president in 1933, he chose her as Secretary of Labor. She was the first woman to serve in a presidential cabinet. Her appointment is usually remembered as a milestone for women, and it was. But that framing is too small for what she did with the job. Calling her a first makes her sound like a symbol, when she was one of the most effective officials of her century."}]]}],"$L2d","$L2e"]}],"$undefined","$L2f"]}]]}]],"$L30"]}]]}]
